  "ownership": [
    "The existing Qt independent-history consumer requires finite detached data; FullLoopResult clones retain complete job/input/stage owners. No speculative instrument API or new public engine path.",
    "Public policy admission bounds independently reducible payload/NCP/protected/decoder counts and a separate byte ceiling; checked fixed/nested likelihood/context accounting precedes observation copies. Wider index arithmetic preserves exact original uniform positions.",
    "Archive clones share only detached immutable observations. Protected copies use the existing empty validated constructor, avoiding hidden pilot-sequence state and full report/vector clones. First actual nonempty decoder context/offset/total remain distinct from physical-cell LLRs.",
    "Live and archived QAM/MER/decisions/soft observations share existing private numerical helpers. Their unchanged 2048-cell/128-decision limits receive common purpose-specific names. Native wrappers perform immutable ownership, selector and JSON conversion only; legacy aliases/stubs mirror the same classes."
  ],
